                  <a href=\"https://www.nwaonline.com/staff/nwa-democrat-gazette\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">NWA Democrat-Gazette</a>\n                                \n                            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n            \n            \n                </p>\n            \n        \n    \n    \n        \n            <p><img src=\"https://wehco.media.clients.ellingtoncms.com/imports/adg/photos/214067637_Bentonville-Garden-Club_ORIG_t320.jpg?fa67021387348b8667950d2a49bd5d6642c5ab68\" alt=\"Jeannine Brazzeal, Bentonville Garden Club youth education chairman, invited Bentonville School District Superintendent Debbie Jones, Executive Administration Assistant to the Superintendent Kimberly Ross and district Chief Operating Officer Tanya Sharp to enjoy Chef Helen Lampkin's garden to table culinary program. Lampkin harvested basil and sage from the students' gardens. She taught the students, guests and volunteers how to prepare potatoes with sage and black bean tacos along with holiday skewers featuring basil leaves, mozzarella pearls and cherry tomatoes with balsamic glaze. Also in attendance were the Washington Junior High School principal, two assistant principals, two sponsoring teachers and a resource officer.\n\n(Submitted Photo)\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"842\" /></p><figcaption>Jeannine Brazzeal, Bentonville Garden Club youth education chairman, invited Bentonville School District Superintendent Debbie Jones, Executive Administration Assistant to the Superintendent Kimberly Ross and district Chief Operating Officer Tanya Sharp to enjoy Chef Helen Lampkin's garden to table culinary program. Lampkin harvested basil and sage from the students' gardens. She taught the students, guests and volunteers how to prepare potatoes with sage and black bean tacos along with holiday skewers featuring basil leaves, mozzarella pearls and cherry tomatoes with balsamic glaze. Also in attendance were the Washington Junior High School principal, two assistant principals, two sponsoring teachers and a resource officer.\n\n(Submitted Photo)</figcaption>\n            \n        \n    \n\n\n\n        \n    \n\n    \n    <p>MILITARY OFFICERS ASSOCIATION OF AMERICA</p>\n          <p><img src=\"https://braze-images.com/appboy/communication/assets/image_assets/images/64710fa5b2c120004fa54eb6/original.png?1685131173\" alt=\"Logo\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" />\n          </p>\n\n          <h2>Subscriber Exclusive</h2>\n          \n          <p>\n            This is subscriber-exclusive reporting from the Northwest Arkansas Democrat-Gazette. It's original coverage you can't get anywhere else.\n          </p>"
